{"id":1490,"date":"2025-10-09T15:06:02","date_gmt":"2025-10-09T13:06:02","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/www.sabourg.com\/?p=1490"},"modified":"2025-10-09T15:06:02","modified_gmt":"2025-10-09T13:06:02","slug":"prince-abbot-giovanni-luca-attends-the-inauguration-ceremony-of-gabons-newly-elected-president-brice-clotaire-oligui-nguema","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/www.sabourg.com\/en\/2025\/10\/09\/prince-abbot-giovanni-luca-attends-the-inauguration-ceremony-of-gabons-newly-elected-president-brice-clotaire-oligui-nguema\/","title":{"rendered":"Prince-Abbot Giovanni Luca attends the inauguration ceremony of Gabon&rsquo;s newly elected President Brice Clotaire Oligui Nguema."},"content":{"rendered":"<div data-olk-copy-source=\"MessageBody\">Le Prince-Abb\u00e9 Giovanni Luca pr\u00e9sent \u00e0 la c\u00e9r\u00e9monie d&rsquo;investiture du nouveau Pr\u00e9sident \u00e9lu du Gabon Brice Clotaire Oligui Nguema.<\/div>\n<div dir=\"auto\"><\/div>\n<div dir=\"auto\">\n<p>In a ceremony marked by solemnity and symbolism, the new President of the Gabonese Republic was sworn in before the country&rsquo;s highest authorities, a delegation of the Gabonese people, and several African heads of state who came to show their support.<\/p>\n<p>President Brice Clotaire Oligui Nguema swore to uphold and enforce the Constitution, preserve national unity, and work tirelessly for peace, justice, and development in Gabon. He extended his hand to all the nation&rsquo;s active forces. He called for \u201ca new era of responsibility, transparency, and collective reconstruction,\u201d while insisting on the need to strengthen regional integration and African cooperation.<\/p>\n<p>The Prince-Abbot of the Principality of Sabourg is on an African tour with a large delegation as part of South-South cooperation.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<div dir=\"auto\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone size-large wp-image-1321\" src=\"https:\/\/www.sabourg.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/05\/1000196479-1024x768.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1024\" height=\"768\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.sabourg.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/05\/1000196479-1024x768.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/www.sabourg.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/05\/1000196479-300x225.jpg 300w, https:\/\/www.sabourg.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/05\/1000196479-768x576.jpg 768w, https:\/\/www.sabourg.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/05\/1000196479-1536x1152.jpg 1536w, https:\/\/www.sabourg.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/05\/1000196479-24x18.jpg 24w, https:\/\/www.sabourg.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/05\/1000196479-36x27.jpg 36w, https:\/\/www.sabourg.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/05\/1000196479-48x36.jpg 48w, https:\/\/www.sabourg.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/05\/1000196479.jpg 1600w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><\/div>\n<div dir=\"auto\"><\/div>\n<div dir=\"auto\"><\/div>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Le Prince-Abb\u00e9 Giovanni Luca pr\u00e9sent \u00e0 la c\u00e9r\u00e9monie d&rsquo;investiture du nouveau Pr\u00e9sident \u00e9lu du Gabon Brice Clotaire Oligui Nguema. In a ceremony marked by solemnity and symbolism, the new President of the Gabonese Republic was sworn in before the country&rsquo;s highest authorities, a delegation of the Gabonese people, and several African heads of state who &hellip;<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":1322,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"footnotes":""},"categories":[133],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-1490","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","category-diplomacy"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.sabourg.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/1490","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.sabourg.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.sabourg.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/post"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/